WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.780
Many organizations require approval checkpoints before software reaches production.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:13.800
Approval workflows help ensure that changes receive appropriate review and oversight before they affect customers, systems, or regulated data.

3
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.400
Approvals are strongest when they are captured in the same delivery workflow that moves the change forward.

4
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:27.060
Review decisions, approver identity, time, scope, and conditions should be recorded as pipeline evidence.

5
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.460
Some environments also require separation of duties.

6
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:38.960
Different people may develop, review, approve, or deploy changes so that one person does not control the entire production path alone.

7
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.200
These controls should be risk-based and practical.

8
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:51.580
The goal is not to slow delivery for its own sake; the goal is to reduce unauthorized or poorly reviewed change while keeping accountable automation in place.
